# Historical gitleaks findings, ignored by fingerprint for CI's full-history scan
# (gh #70). `gitleaks git . --config .gitleaks.toml` already drops every finding
# whose secret VALUE matches an allowlist regex in .gitleaks.toml, across every
# commit that literal ever appeared in — which covers the README placeholder and
# the fixtures .gitleaks.toml already lists. This file exists only for a finding
# that config can't reach: a fake credential in a test file that no longer exists
# in the working tree, so there is no live line to attach a `gitleaks:allow`
# comment to and no current file for .gitleaks.toml's allowlist to describe.
#
# Regenerate by running, from a full clone:
#   gitleaks git . --redact --no-banner --config .gitleaks.toml \
#     --report-format json --report-path /tmp/gitleaks-report.json
# and copying the Fingerprint field of whatever still appears.
#
# api_key fixture asserting the analyzer never leaks a credential into its output —
# daemon/tests/integration/test_analyzer_integration.py, introduced at e2ffa94 (the
# initial commit) and removed at 6ea0b86 (`refactor: remove dead analyzer.py code
# and improve LLM prompt structure`), so it exists only in history.
